      "problem": "Identify the surface $2{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}-4x-y-16z-12=0.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we complete the square in the $x$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}-4x-y-16z-12 & =0 \\\\ 2({x}^{2}-2x)-4({z}^{2}+4z)-y-12 & =0 \\\\ 2[(x-1)^{2}-1]-4[(z+2)^{2}-4]-y-12 & =0 \\\\ 2(x-1)^{2}-2-4(z+2)^{2}+16-y-12 & =0 \\\\ 2(x-1)^{2}-4(z+2)^{2}-y+2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-1)^{2}-4(z+2)^{2}-y+2 & =0 \\\\ 2(x-1)^{2}-4(z+2)^{2} & =y-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(1,2,-2).$",
